[2.246992, "o", "Model       gpt-5-mini, prompt v4 (cached response)\r\r\nReport?     yes\r\r\nSummary     An insufficient session expiration vulnerability in the ArubaOS CLI allows an attacker to keep a session running on an affected device after the removal of the impacted account.\r\r\nProduct     ArubaOS (unspecified versions)\r\r\nCWE         CWE-306\r\r\nCVSS 3.1    CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N  ->  4.3 Medium (provisional: mostly inferred)\r\r\nInferred    AC, UI, S, C, A\r\r\nConfidence  low\r\r\nFlags       cvss_provisional\r\r\nNext step   Validate affected ArubaOS versions, reproduce by creating a CLI session, deleting the account, and confirming session persistence; collect exact conditions (remote/local, required privileges) and prepare coordinated disclosure and patch.\r\r\nEvidence\r\r\n  - High-level description of the vulnerability: \"An insufficient session expiration vulnerability exists in the ArubaOS command line interface.\"\r\r\n  - Impact description: \"Successful exploitation of this vulnerability allows an attacker to keep a session running on an affected device after the removal of the impacted account\"\r\r\n\r\r\n[a]pprove  [e]dit  [r]eject > "]
